@startuml system_seq_authority
!include ../style.iuml
autonumber

participant "Central Harness\n(shared clock)" as H
participant "CTC Office" as CTC
participant "Track Controller\n(SW Green / HW Red)" as TC
participant "Track Model" as TM
participant "Train Model" as TrM
participant "Train Controller\n(SW Green / HW Red)" as TrC

note over H
  Every tick the harness sends dt and the simulation time to every
  module at once; each module steps on the outputs of the tick before,
  mapped by the harness (D005, D017). One tick is 0.1 s.
end note

== tick k ==
H -> CTC : STEP: occupancy, switch states, ready per line
CTC -> CTC : route the train; authority = blocks it\nmay still enter (D013), never into an occupied,\nclosed or failed block; speed it can stop from
CTC --> H : suggestion for the train's block\nand the next block on its route

== tick k+1 ==
H -> H : map per train to per block;\ndrop the train ID
H -> TC : STEP: suggestions, closures, occupancy
TC -> TC : PLC scan on two channels:\nAUTH_n passes or withholds authority;\nspeed capped at the block's limit
TC --> H : track circuit per block,\nswitch, signal, crossing commands

== tick k+2 ==
H -> TM : STEP: track circuits and commands
TM -> TM : set switches, signals, crossings;\nplace the command on the train's block
TM --> H : track signal for the train in the block;\nclear the block's values to zero

== tick k+3 ==
H -> TrM : STEP: track signal, terrain, beacons
TrM -> TrM : physics step; pass the commanded\nspeed and authority through
TrM --> H : position, block change,\ncommanded speed and authority

== tick k+4 ==
H -> TrC : STEP: commanded speed, authority,\nsignal aspect ahead
TrC -> TrC : regulate to the commanded speed;\nbrake to stop within the authority
TrC --> H : power command, brakes
H -> TrM : (tick k+5) power and brake commands
@enduml
